  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 10.75,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: on the route point the rider is right, but not to the extent asked, and the correct figure is the one both parties' surviving claims converge on.\n\nRoute deviation. The GPS trace EV-GPS-00106 (weight 1.0) measures 10.78 km for this trip. Against the booked optimal of 7.2 km on the trip record EV-TRIP-00106 (weight 1.0), that is an excess of 3.58 km, or 49.72% — above the 20% and 0.8 km establishment gates of POL-RD-01, so a deviation is ESTABLISHED. It stops just short of the 50% and 8.0 km materiality gates, so it is not a MATERIAL deviation: the POL-RD-06 repeat-deviation check and its full-refund uplift are not engaged, and in any event the citable fields show deviation_flags_90d 0 against 96 completed_trips_90d, i.e. no pattern. The trace is not impaired under POL-RD-07 (169 fixes, 10 s sampling, 100% coverage, no gaps), so the measured excess stands and no independent corroboration is needed.\n\nMoney. The fare is METERED, so POL-RD-02 applies. recomputed_fare = (3.80 base + 0.75 x 7.2 km + 0.28 x 19.0 min) x surge 1.0 read from the fare_breakdown + 0.80 platform fee + 0.00 ERP on the optimal route = 15.32. Refund = 26.04 charged_total - 15.32 = 10.72, rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05 = 10.75. That is 41.17% of the charge, well below the 90% share that would convert it into a full refund, so the rider's request for the whole 26.04 is not granted and the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 10.75.\n\nWhy the $5.50 of ERP is not added on top. Both gantries — CTE (Braddell Rd towards City) SGD 3.00 and CTE (Chin Swee Rd tunnel) SGD 2.50 — are off the optimal route, and the 15.32 recomputed fare already includes only on-optimal-route gantries (0.00 here). POL-RD-09(1) comprehends that ERP inside the 10.72 difference; itemising it separately and adding it would produce 16.25, which is precisely the double count the clause forbids. No standalone pass-through correction is available either: both gantries are matched by trace fixes within the 250 m radius (0.0 m and 24.1 m) and there is no airport surcharge, so POL-RD-09(4) finds no billing-integrity defect.\n\nWhy the excess is not reduced. The single chat message EV-CHAT-00106 is the rider's own objection at 08:46:30 — 'why we at havelock? bugis is behind us' — not an instruction, and its waypoint_hint is null, so POL-RD-04 and POL-RD-14 leave the measured excess intact. No pickup or dropoff amendment exists (POL-RD-05), and the vehicle is not pooled (POL-RD-12).\n\nEscalation and process. No POL-RD-10 trigger fires: the identifiers match across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown (TRP-00106), the trace is unimpaired, timestamps are consistent, and the refund is far below SGD 150.00. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00106-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0); the claim that discussed it was discarded by the referee and neither side's surviving claims rely on it, so it does not carry this ruling. One procedural note: the monetary effect of SGD 10.75 exceeds the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so under POL-GEN-05 the ruling issues but the amount is held and placed in the human queue for release rather than paid out automatically. Either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04."
  },
