    "explanation": "Both parties' kept claims converge on the same figures, and the tribunal adopts that common ground.\n\nTHE TRIP. Trip TRP-00106 ran from Blk 79 Toa Payoh Central to Bugis Junction on 17 July 2026 and was charged $26.04 on a metered fare. The trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown all carry trip id TRP-00106 and open at the same pickup event (08:35:15), so the rider's initial burden under POL-RD-08 is discharged.\n\nDEVIATION. Under POL-RD-01 the governing measurement is gps_trace.trace_distance_km = 10.78 km, not the trip record's rounded 10.8 km convenience copy. Against the booked optimal of 7.2 km this is an excess of 3.58 km, or 49.72% of optimal. Both establishment gates pass (greater than 0.8 km and greater than 20%), so a deviation is ESTABLISHED. Neither materiality gate passes (49.72% is not greater than 50%, and 3.58 km is not greater than 8.0 km), so the deviation is not MATERIAL and the POL-RD-06 uplift is not engaged. The driver's profile shows 0 deviation_flags_90d against 96 completed_trips_90d, so no repeat-deviation pattern exists on the citable fields in any event. The rider's demand for the whole $26.04 is therefore rejected; the correct remedy is the POL-RD-02 partial.\n\nREFUND. The fare is METERED, so the remedy is arithmetic under POL-RD-02: recomputed_fare = (3.80 base + 0.75 × 7.2 km + 0.28 × 19.0 min) × 1.0 surge (read from the fare_breakdown) + 0.80 platform fee + 0.00 ERP on the optimal route = 15.32. Refund = charged_total 26.04 − 15.32 = 10.72, rounded up to the nearest $0.05 = $10.75. That is 41.2% of the charge, below the 90% share that would convert it to a FULL_REFUND, so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND of $10.75.\n\nERP. The $5.50 of ERP (CTE Braddell Rd $3.00, CTE Chin Swee tunnel $2.50) lies off the optimal route, which carries $0.00. Under POL-RD-09(1) that $5.50 is already comprehended inside the $10.72 difference, because the recomputed fare includes only on-optimal-route gantries; adding it again would produce $16.25, the double count POL-RD-09(1) forbids. It is itemised for transparency and is not added on top. Both gantries are matched by the trace (nearest fixes 0.0 m and 24.1 m, inside the 250 m radius) and no airport surcharge was charged, so no POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity defect arises and no referral is produced.\n\nNO EXONERATION. The chat log holds one rider message at 08:46:30 ('why we at havelock? bugis is behind us'). It is a contemporaneous objection, not a detour instruction, and waypoint_hint is null, so POL-RD-04 cannot apply and, per POL-RD-14, no distance is excluded. There is no amendment under POL-RD-05 (all amendment fields null) and no pooling under POL-RD-12 (vehicle_type is RYDE_TAXI, solo_optimal_distance_km null), so the booked 7.2 km optimal stands. No traffic advisory covers this window, and no external-cause exoneration under POL-RD-03 was asserted.\n\nESCALATION. The trace is unimpaired: 169 fixes at 10 s spacing, 100% coverage, no gaps, max_gap 0.0 — POL-RD-07(a)–(c) are not met, so POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged. Trip ids match, timestamps agree, and the refund is far below $150 and below charged_total; no POL-RD-10 trigger fires.\n\nEXECUTION AND APPEAL. The monetary effect of $10.75 exceeds the $8.00 execution threshold on this policy file, so under POL-GEN-05 the ruling issues but is not executed automatically: the amount is held and placed in the human queue for release. Independently of that queue, this is a provisional ruling and either party may appeal once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04.\n\nCONFIDENCE. The deciding facts rest on the trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown, all at weight_multiplier 1.0, so confidence is set at 0.90."
